fix(imports): fix a static import bug (#1060)

Here is the root cause:
The `MinimalImportScanner` used an unordered `HashSet<String>` to collect the qualified name tokens (package segments) leading up to a field/method reference, and then checked if **any** token in that set matched a field, method, or local variable name in scope to decide whether the reference was already accessible without an import. Because a `Set` has no guaranteed order, this check could match on an irrelevant package-name token instead of the actual meaningful token (the immediately enclosing class/type name), producing incorrect results. Additionally, the package-hierarchy traversal loop did not stop at the top-level (unnamed) package, so it could continue adding an extra/incorrect token to the qualified-name collection. Together, these two issues caused the scanner to fail to recognize that a private static field access (e.g., `STREAM_BUFFER_LENGTH`) occurred within the **same class** where it was declared, incorrectly concluding that a static import was required, thus generating an unnecessary `import static ...` statement.

